Results on this host:

* Focused tests: **7 passed**.
* The 30+20 and 1.4+1.4 zero-spin support fixtures agree with the contract
  at about `7e-14` seconds or better.  The support calculation uses positive
  TaylorT2 terms through 2PN, the independently derived `54πM` orbital period
  at `r=9M`, and 11 fundamental 22-mode damping times.
* The analytic half-cosine samples for `n=4` are
  `[0, 0.1464466094, 0.5, 0.8535533906, 1, ...]`.  A synthetic 527-sample
  paired fixture trims seven exact suffix zeros after filtering and reports
  taper counts `(first, second-begin, second-end) = (503, 125, 64)`.
* Against SciPy's independently constructed standard eighth-order SOS
  Butterworth filter (same prewarped corner and section order), the Torch
  recurrence has relative L2 error `1.214e-15` and maximum absolute error
  `4.441e-15` for a deterministic length-4096 vector in float64.
* The diagnostic run takes about `229 ms` for the four-section forward/reverse
  recurrence at `N=4096` and `6.75 s` at `N=120000`; cost is linear in samples
  and sections, with batch entries evaluated in parallel.  A float32 batched
  TD→FD check produced finite outputs and a finite gradient through the
  waveform and `tc` phase.
* Fourier checks cover explicit `f_max/delta_f` sizing (`100/1 → N=256`,
  Nyquist `128 Hz`) and automatic strict-power-of-two sizing (`n=8 → N=16`).

## Provenance

The timing expression was derived from the standard PN phasing equations in
Blanchet, *Living Reviews in Relativity* (2014),
<https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.1528>.  The fundamental Kerr 22 QNM fit is from
Berti, Cardoso & Will, Appendix E/Table VIII,
<https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0512160>.  The equal-mass aligned remnant-spin
linear estimate is from Tichy & Marronetti,
<https://arxiv.org/abs/0807.2985>.  No constants were fitted to LAL; public
SciPy was used only as an independent numerical filter check, and no native
EOB trajectory was started.
